{"name":"Chaparral","hex":"#e5d0b0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chaparral","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A neighbourhood in south-east Calgary, Alberta, Canada.","A census-designated place in Doña Ana County and Otero County, New Mexico, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chaparral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chaparral","blocks":[{"text":"Chaparral is a shrubland plant community found primarily in California, southern Oregon, and northern Baja California, part of the California floristic province. It is shaped by a Mediterranean climate and infrequent, high-intensity crown fires. Many chaparral shrubs have hard sclerophyllous evergreen leaves, in contrast to the soft-leaved, drought-deciduous, coastal sage scrub that is often found on drier, southern-facing slopes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Chaparral1.jpg/330px-Chaparral1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaparral","wikidata":"Q842123"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Guatay_old_growth_carpet.jpg/500px-Guatay_old_growth_carpet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Guatay_old_growth_carpet.jpg/1280px-Guatay_old_growth_carpet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Guatay_old_growth_carpet.jpg/500px-Guatay_old_growth_carpet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old-growth chaparral more than a century old","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuatay_old_growth_carpet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/CSS_with_LR-1b_x.jpg/500px-CSS_with_LR-1b_x.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars